WEBVTT

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:10.900
Yugi Muto assembled the Millennium Puzzle and became the guardian of the Shadow Games.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.180
Pegasus has a Millennium Item of his own - the Millennium Eye.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.680
Yugi accepts Pegasus's challenge and goes to Duelist Kingdom.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.740
Pegasus stole his grandfather Sugoroku's soul, and Yugi intends to rescue him.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.850
He battles alongside his trusted friends and with his other self.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.300
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.210
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.960
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.660
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.760
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.130
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:20.060
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.310
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:33.580
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.320
What is truly precious?

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:49.820
Yugi, you're about to feel a duel that will turn your blood into ice.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.770
Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon!

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.540
This is the fusion of three Blue-Eyes?

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.800
Here comes Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon's attack!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.520
Ultimate Burst!

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.760
My victory is assured.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.830
I won't give up!

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.800
Good.  Oppose me to the end.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:40.270
Yugi, even if you muster up all your strength, I'll crush you easily!

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.880
I bet everything on this draw!

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:52.380
Kuribohs Multiply!
Shocking Finale

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.860
Even if you play it in defense position, you're only extending your suffering.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.440
Do you actually believe you can turn this duel around?

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:25.760
Kaiba, I drew the strongest card remaining in my deck.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.420
What?

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.420
And the card is...

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.740
Here I go!

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.170
I play Kuriboh in attack position!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.080
How ridiculous!

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.710
Kuriboh is a weak monster with only 300 attack points!

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.720
What's that tiny, weak-looking monster?

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:00.860
Yugi, you're allowed to give up.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.320
But to think that you'll play such a weak monster.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:12.420
That weak, low-Level monster has the fewest attack points in all of Duel Monsters.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:16.200
I've never met anyone who keeps that card in their deck.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:23.940
Yugi, I won't forgive you for insulting me with that card and dishonoring our duel!

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.340
You're wrong, Kaiba.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.450
This card is my trump card!

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.450
I'll use it to destroy your Ultimate Dragon!

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.180
What?  That's nonsense!

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:39.460
That pathetic monster can't destroy my Ultimate Dragon!

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.460
Here I go!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:45.140
I activate the spell card Multiply.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:50.160
This card endlessly multiplies a monster with 500-or-fewer attack points.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.940
What's this?

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.280
That weak monster is multiplying?

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:07.510
It's true that my monster is weak because it only has 300 attack points, but you shouldn't underestimate it.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:11.790
Its hidden abilities are superior to those of high-Level monsters!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:17.500
Nonsense!  My Ultimate Dragon will burn all those runts together!

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.300
Attack!  Ultimate Burst!

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.170
What?

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:28.240
Ultimate Dragon's attack didn't work?

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:36.650
Those weaklings' effects make them self-destruct the moment that they're attacked?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:42.820
That's right.  Kuriboh self-destructs the moment it touches your monster or its attack.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:47.560
Which means your Ultimate Dragon's attack can't affect all the Kuribohs!

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.630
Damn!  And it's such a weakling!

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.630
And they're multiplying even more.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:00.140
My Kuriboh-Multiply combo doesn't lose its strength unless they're all destroyed.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:05.640
So you must destroy all the Kuribohs to reduce my life points to 0.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.180
But before that happens...

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:11.150
I'll play my second trump card this turn!

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.390
Your second trump card?

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:18.560
Here I go!  This is the three-card combo that will bring your Ultimate Dragon down!

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.910
Mammoth Graveyard, Polymerization and Spell Shattering Arrow!

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.800
Spell Shattering Arrow?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:32.570
Spell Shattering Arrow allows me to give my spell card's effect to your monster.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.960
I use the spell card Polymerization.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:45.050
I fuse Mammoth Graveyard with your Ultimate Dragon, which you created by fusing three Blue-Eyes together.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.050
What?

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:04.320
What's going on?

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.380
Blue-Eyes White Dragon is Light Attribute.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:16.260
So when I fuse Ultimate Dragon with Mammoth Graveyard, a Zombie-Type Monster with Dark Attribute...

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:20.050
...the two Attributes oppose each other, and its body begins to decay.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.290
My Ultimate Dragon is decaying.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.660
Mammoth Graveyard has 1200 attack points.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:34.070
That means Ultimate Dragon loses 1200 attack points every turn.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.800
I've turned the tables, Kaiba!

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:45.260
I have Negate Attack in my deck to stop attack damage, but it can't stop the decay from the fusion.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.760
All right!  Yugi's combo brought him back from certain defeat!

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.240
You can defeat Kaiba!

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.840
Yugi!

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.330
Did you see that, Kaiba?

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:56.790
Yugi has no weaknesses!

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:03.800
No matter how difficult the situation, I always believed in the strength of the other Yugi.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:10.340
Kaiba fused three Blue-Eyes, but Yugi fought back by using another fusion.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.960
Fighting fire with fire.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.200
Yugi is very clever.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.020
The duel hasn't been decided yet!

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.360
Ultimate Dragon, attack!

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.860
Ultimate Burst!

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:33.860
It's pointless.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:41.100
My monster keeps multiplying, so it's impossible to destroy them all.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.480
Those little runts!

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.980
I draw one card and end my turn.

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:59.460
Yugi is letting his turns pass by.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.680
Attack!  Ultimate Burst!

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:11.820
It's no good.  It doesn't work.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:17.670
I can't attack, and Ultimate Dragon loses attack points each turn.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:20.440
I end my turn.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.680
Kaiba, you're finished!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.220
Am I going to lose?

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.120
Impossible.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:38.400
Mokuba!

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.000
If I lose, Mokuba will...

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.620
Big brother!

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:52.420
Big brother, save me!

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:54.940
Mokuba!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:59.450
Big brother, save me...

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:01.950
Mokuba!

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.780
Mokuba!

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.260
Big brother!

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.460
Big brother...

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:13.480
Mokuba!

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.510
Why didn't you save him?

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:33.010
Why weren't you willing to sacrifice your life to save him?

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:50.260
Mokuba...

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:59.570
Is Kaiba going to pass his turn without doing anything?

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:03.460
Kaiba is just standing there completely spaced out.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:05.580
He has accepted his defeat.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:12.580
As his turns pass without doing anything, Ultimate Dragon's attack points keep dropping.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:28.340
All right!  Ultimate Dragon's attack points have dropped far enough that I can destroy it!

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.880
My turn!  I play a new card!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:51.890
Celtic Guardian, attack Ultimate Dragon!

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:01.970
All right!

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.470
The other Yugi is really strong!

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:09.200
Ultimate Dragon isn't dead yet.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:19.220
I see.  Since Ultimate Dragon is a fusion of three Blue-Eyes, each head has its own attack points.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:23.490
But I can clearly reduce Kaiba's life points.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:29.800
When Celtic Guardian attacks another head next turn, I win!

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:33.380
Yugi...

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.300
The game is only beginning.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:40.740
Your attack took away 500 life points.

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:45.910
I'll equate each square on the floor as 100 life points.

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:51.280
I'll walk backwards equal to the life points I lost.

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:52.050
What?

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:55.620
500 points means I walk five squares back.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:02.570
Hey!

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.530
What's he doing?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.780
Kaiba!

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.330
I can't step back any further.

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:50.520
If you attack me next turn, I will truly lose my life.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:51.980
Kaiba!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.710
If I die in a duel, I'll be satisfied!

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:03.820
Kaiba, stop it!  This is dangerous!

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.090
That punk!

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:07.740
This isn't fair, Kaiba!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.600
You're bluffing so that Yugi can't make his final attack?

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:17.340
But what if it isn't a bluff?

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:19.200
That's impossible.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:25.060
In order to win, the other fiercer Yugi may actually attack!

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:30.220
I'll never figure out what he's thinking!

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:35.520
Yugi, the next turn will reveal what kind of duelist you truly are.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.400
Games are like opposing mirrors.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:41.460
If I was the other person, how would I avoid my own attack?

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:46.100
By becoming your opponent, you anticipate how to attack.

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.700
When you understand yourself, you achieve victory.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:55.210
If I were in your place, I would hurtle you to the valley below without hesitation.

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:59.240
But the duel still isn't over.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:02.180
I'll draw a card this turn.

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:07.780
My card is Monster Reborn.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:12.730
I'll use this card to resurrect the Blue-Eyes head that was just destroyed.

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:15.460
What?  Blue-Eyes' head?

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:21.970
One Blue-Eyes with the usual 3000 attack points has been resurrected.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:26.860
Since it was part of a fusion when it was destroyed, I can't resurrect it independently.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:30.040
It also can't attack until the next turn.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.680
Yugi, it's your turn!

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.350
That was pointless.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:40.650
No matter what monster he resurrects, his attack can't get through my shield of Kuribohs.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:47.240
If I destroy one of the heads with 900 attack points this turn, I win.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:49.660
But what will happen to Kaiba's life?

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:54.430
Yugi, use your card to finish me!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:57.580
I...

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:03.120
I...

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:10.520
I can't afford to lose!

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:17.520
The look on his face means that the other Yugi chooses victory even if it means sending Kaiba plummeting!

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.330
Here I go, Kaiba!

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:20.890
Celtic Guardian!

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.700
Yugi!  No!

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.400
Stop!

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:37.500
Yugi, return to your old self!

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:39.820
Yugi!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:16:59.930
I win.

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:02.300
Burst Stream!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:30.460
Master Pegasus, the battle between Yugi and Kaiba has just ended.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.860
Seto Kaiba is the winner.

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.970
I know.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:39.440
Is it okay to bring Seto Kaiba into the castle?

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.610
That's no problem.

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:43.300
I'll do it right away.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:49.500
Good job, Kaiba boy.

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:54.350
As you wish, I'll be your next opponent.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.600
In a Shadow Game.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:11.550
What happened?

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:15.610
That kid could've won the game, but he threw it away.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.310
Yugi!

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.400
I couldn't do it.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:33.060
If I continued the game, Kaiba could've died!

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:35.290
Yugi, you...

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:38.430
You gave up victory to save Kaiba.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:44.440
Since the battle was out-of-control, that was the only way you could stop it.

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:47.680
I'm scared.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.800
I'm scared of these games and my other self!

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:56.020
I'm sorry, Yugi.

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:00.320
But you're not wrong, Yugi.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:05.280
You showed weakness in the end, Yugi.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:11.680
If you were willing to send me into the abyss, you would've won.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.330
As a duelist, you made a foolish choice.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:16.070
You're wrong!

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.810
You're the one who lost the game, Kaiba!

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:21.900
What?

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:28.450
Kaiba, you tried to throw away your most valuable chip: your life.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:30.840
You lost to yourself!

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:34.690
You didn't have the courage to face yourself to the end!

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:44.700
Real courage is to protect your chip - your life - no matter what the situation.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.030
You lost when you threw it away!

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:51.820
Yugi saved your chip of life!

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.280
That was an interesting show.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:13.880
With ten Star Chips, the gate lock is released.

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:22.840
Pegasus, I'm coming!

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:38.170
Shocked, Yugi has lost his way.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.680
No matter what we say, he won't listen to us.

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:47.480
Mai offers to return the Star Chips she borrowed, but Yugi won't take them.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:49.600
That means Yugi will be eliminated!

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:53.570
Mai, wager those Star Chips in a duel against me!

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:56.260
I'll be the one to take Yugi to the castle!

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:59.860
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Duel of Tears!
Shining Friendship

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.510
Duel, standby!

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:12.160
The flask glistens

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:20.010
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:28.980
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:36.760
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:42.590
Shower of happiness

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:46.700
I will shower you with it

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:54.970
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:59.210
Shower of happiness

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:03.340
You are not alone

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:10.060
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
